      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm a little confused! PhysBones' fidelity is an improvement over Dynamic Bones in essentially every way, while also simultaneously being more performant by several orders of magnitude. \nI'll try my best to understand what you're trying to communicate, but I have some questions.\n> [PhysBones] looks really calculated and not simulated.\nI'm unsure what you mean by this! Can you clarify what \"calculated and not simulated\" means? Can you give visual examples?\n> The things that made dynamic bones look good are not implemented in physicsBones\nCan you name specific things or features that are missing? Inside Colliders are missing from PB, but we're likely to add them. I get the feeling that's not what you're talking about, though.\nFor feedback and feature requests, it behooves you to be as clear as possible!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
