      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: \nHey! I will try to my best to explain the questions.\n> [PhysBones] looks really calculated and not simulated:\nI made a little video under here of PhysBones compared to dynamic bones. What I noticed is that PhysBones work like in a group/chunk where the calculations are little spread out over the multiple bones.\nDynamic bones looked way more organic and this way more simulated. \nIt can be that I just didn't have the right settings for it. While testing I noticed that the Immobile is a compination off stiffness & inert?\nhttps://youtu.be/yNp0TrGYjQw\n> The things that made dynamic bones look good are not implemented in physicsBones\nDynamic bone has a smooth ending calculation so for example when long hair moves you have to force of the movement applied to it and it smooth the hair out once you stand still. With PhysBones I got the feeling it was really quickly to just become stiff/hanging at the back without the smooth transition from moving to stopping.\nWith long hair I really mean long long hair (12 bone spread at the back with 8 bone going down every line).\nThis hair is meant to be really long & flowy. When I tried this with Physbones to ended up looking really stiff and not really flowy.\nJust like before I might have the wrong settings for this.\nI hope I explained this now a little better if you need anything more please let me know I will try to setup multiple test & result as needed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
