      "value": "@{5f3046762b921879a5151868|full_name}: For the video, I think part of what you're seeing is the rotation of DynBones as it rolls the chain back out, because it incorrectly twisted it during the pull. PB never incorrectly rotates the bone when pulling, so it doesn't \"untwist\". I'm making a lot of guesses here, but IMO the PB in your video is closer to how a chain should act than DB.\nIn other words, I think the behavior you're observing in the tail in DB is actually less realistic, and PB's implementation has fixed it.\nAs far as how \"flowy\" the hair looks, I agree with Blizzball-- try adjusting your Pull value, and using a curve to lessen pull over the length of the hair chain.\nThe video very much helped for the first. For the second, can you provide another?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
