      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: \nHey here I got a video for the long flowy hair tried some with the curve module~\nOnly downside is that the dynamic bones use force & gravity (force not existing in physics bones)\nhttps://youtu.be/z5Fwbl63IFU\nhttps://youtu.be/BOaZsKMKKLk\nDid experimentation with movement and rotation.\nWhile looking at it couple of times there is more flowy ness in the dynamic bones hair and it stayed little bit more spaced between the hair strand of becoming more like a singler line. \n \nThat's being said there wasn't a floor collider and the hair of dynamic bones does strange things because of this because of force & gravity combined~\nNow I played bit more with it think can say you might be able to get something similar but you need to adjust everything manually (almost from scratch), using the 'auto converter' works maybe only for the radius but converting the physics over doesn't work really well.\nHope I provided enough information, if you need anything more please let me know I will try to setup multiple test & result as needed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
