  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would like a option for avatar to run a more realistic simulated bones from physics bones. Currently they looking like its run by calculation not giving a impression to simulation (what dynamic bones does).\nI know the point of physicsBones was making it more optimized. But what I have seen so far its made so it can be runned on Quest and not directed to PC VR, making it lower quality simulations of physics to make it run on quest.\nPC (highend) can easily run dynamic bones in the 'old' update. Even that VRC declined to update Dynamic bones to V1.3 (That was more optimized then we got now).\nphysicsBones is a downgrade for highend pc's. It looks really calculated and not simulated.\nThe things that made dynamic bones look good are not implemented in physicsBones.\nWhat I want as request (if you didn't see what I try to point out)\nMake 2 versions, one for quest avatars and one for PC VR. Having PC VR more options in the SDK for more realistic simulation like Dynamic bones.",
